  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_019, a multimodal multiprofile PCA/ResNet weighted-fusion model with avgpool aggregation, achieving the best validation accuracy and F1. RNA-only results suggest multiprofile avgpool can help, but it is still unclear whether multiprofile aggregation is actually needed in the multimodal setting or whether the gain comes mainly from adding image features. Config_017 tests the same multimodal weighted PCA/ResNet setup with singleprofile, directly clarifying whether the multiprofile/aggregation component is driving the improvement or whether a simpler singleprofile model is sufficient. This is the best next experiment because it is a clean comparison within the currently strongest family, avoids assuming that multiprofile complexity is necessary, and will guide whether to keep or simplify the architecture before exploring new encoders or aggregators."
}

